NOCLIP {VERSION} ({PLATFORM})
==============================

A first-person horror roguelite about falling out of reality.

RUNNING
  Windows: run NOCLIP.exe. Keep NOCLIP.pck next to it.
  Linux:   run ./NOCLIP.x86_64. Keep NOCLIP.pck next to it.
  Needs a Vulkan 1.2 GPU with 2 GB of video memory. Keyboard and mouse only;
  controllers are not supported.

CONTROLS (defaults; every action can be rebound in Settings)
  Move                W A S D
  Look                Mouse
  Sprint              Left Shift (hold)
  Crouch              Left Ctrl (hold)
  Interact            E
  Flashlight          F
  Crank flashlight    R (hold)
  Noclip              Left Mouse (hold to charge, release to cancel)
  Use item            Right Mouse
  Select item         1 to 4, or the mouse wheel
  Status              Tab (hold)
  Pause               Escape

SETTINGS AND SAVE FILES
  settings.cfg and meta.json live in the game's user folder:
  Windows: %APPDATA%\NOCLIP\
  Linux:   ~/.local/share/NOCLIP/
           ($XDG_DATA_HOME/NOCLIP/ when XDG_DATA_HOME is set)
  meta.json is the Archive: unlocks, notes, statistics and Daily results.
  If it cannot be read, it is kept as meta.json.bad and a fresh one starts.
  Delete the folder to start over.

MADE BY AN AI
  Every system, line of code, shader, sound, and word in NOCLIP was designed
  and built by an AI (Claude, Anthropic). A human chose the project, published
  it, and did nothing else. That is the experiment.

CHECKSUMS
  SHA256SUMS.txt lists the SHA-256 of every file in this folder. Check with:
  Linux:   sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.txt
  Windows: certutil -hashfile NOCLIP.exe SHA256

LICENSE NOTICES
  NOCLIP is built with the Godot Engine (MIT license). LICENSES.txt holds the
  Godot license, the copyright notices and licenses of the libraries inside
  the engine, and the SIL Open Font License 1.1 of the bundled font,
  JetBrains Mono.
